I recheck my code and my data, and I think my code and data are already correct.
I try GPA with semi-landmarks and the result is the same as above which is the order that affects the result.
```
gpa <- gpagen(femurdata[,,c(1,2)], curves = sliders)
gpa1 <- gpagen(femurdata[,,c(2,1)], curves = sliders)
# the result gpa!=gpa1
```
however, when I try GPA and treat semi-landmarks as landmarks, the result from different order data are similar.
```
gpa <- gpagen(femurdata[,,c(1,2)])
gpa1 <- gpagen(femurdata[,,c(2,1)])
# the result gpa==gpa1
```
Are semi-landmarks affect the result? why? (which I think the result should be similar)

The following code is the code that I use to define the semi-landmarks. Are they have anything wrong?
```{r}
nfi <- 9   # number of landmarks
Fm.fix <- 1:9
Fm.cur1 <- c((nfi+1):(nfi+20))
Fm.cur2 <- c((nfi+21):(nfi+23))
Fm.cur3 <- c((nfi+24):(nfi+29))
Fm.cur4 <- c((nfi+30):(nfi+33))
Fm.cur5 <- c((nfi+34):(nfi+53))
Fm.cur6 <- c((nfi+54):(nfi+60))
Fm.cur7 <- c((nfi+61):(nfi+65))
Fm.curves <- c(Fm.cur1,Fm.cur2,Fm.cur3,Fm.cur4,Fm.cur5,Fm.cur6,Fm.cur7)
sliders<-rbind(define.sliders(Fm.cur1),define.sliders(Fm.cur2),define.sliders(Fm.cur3),define.sliders(Fm.cur4),define.sliders(Fm.cur5),define.sliders(Fm.cur6),define.sliders(Fm.cur7))
```
